From 612aba6db9678394d0c2eb4d95a5cbf750f1a6d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Roland <rob@retronauts.org>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:25:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] implement the l4re Platform against L4Re

Console output on handles 1-2 goes to the L4Re log capability, Time
reads the KIP clock and Delay sleeps with an IPC timeout. Memory,
getenv and exit still come from libc. Files, directories and terminals
need Plaid's VFS and fail with Linux errno values until it exists:
lookups with ENOENT, creation with ENOSYS, terminal control with
ENOTTY. There is no wall clock yet, so the time of day reads as zero.

PlatformNativel4re is empty; Platform no longer imports it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
